        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(mobile): default pairing to full node access",
        "body": "Closes #105843\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe official iOS and Android apps connected as nodes, but mobile QR/setup-code pairing only handed them a bounded operator credential. Users therefore missed normal full node/operator behavior unless they manually approved more access, and native settings did not explain the limited state or upgrade path.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nOfficial mobile pairing now issues the node credential plus full operator access by default. Full access is restricted to the exact official mobile bootstrap profile and matching native client metadata; arbitrary bootstrap profiles remain bounded. Control UI and `openclaw qr --limited` preserve an explicit limited-access fallback, and rescanning a Full access code upgrades an existing limited mobile pairing.\n\n## User Impact\n\niOS and Android pair as fully usable nodes by default. Operators who prefer least privilege can choose Limited access, while both native settings screens show Full/Limited state and tell limited users to rescan a Full access QR code to upgrade.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxckgwbgms3d3n72gc5kpkky` (`violet-barnacle-a620`): `pnpm check:changed` passed all selected core, core-test, UI, extension, app, and docs lanes in 14m07s.\n- Gateway authorization suites: 82/82 passed; includes full handoff, bounded limited credential verification, and same-identity limited-to-full upgrade.\n- CLI setup: 24/24 passed; black-box default/`--limited` exercise reported Full/Limited respectively, issued non-empty distinct setup codes, and exposed no credential values.\n- Control UI Chromium E2E passed; recorded request sequence `full -> limited -> full -> full`, proving regeneration and reset-on-reopen. Before/after artifacts retained in the Testbox run.\n- Android: `pnpm android:lint` and `pnpm android:test` passed (34 Gradle tasks). Native i18n generation/check, protocol/Swift generation checks, and targeted SwiftFormat passed.\n- Fresh Autoreview slices: core, authorization-sensitive gateway handler, native apps, Control UI, and regression tests all clean after accepted findings were fixed.\n- Source-blind behavior validation found no product failures across executable CLI/UI/upgrade paths. Direct iOS runtime proof was blocked because the approved Apple host was unreachable over SSH; macOS CI remains the Apple gate.\n",
        "branch": "codex/mobile-node-full-access",
